WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.240
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.250
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.140
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.930
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.800
I'm an SDF member.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.720
I do not want to harbour any doubts...

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.970
...about rescuing a fellow human being.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:43.140
What I saw on land wasn't just history.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.140
But the lives of the people in this era.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.520
It didn't make any difference...

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.560
...whether they were Japanese or American.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:57.440
To the crew of the Mirai...

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.780
The blood of all men are the same!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.910
They are all red!

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.910
For the sake of one life, we have sacrificed eight.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.840
The Will of Lieutenant Okamura

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.760
You're just like a baby, XO.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.180
You slept the whole day.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.430
I'm giving you an injection, hold on a minute.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.640
How is Officer Yanagi?

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.440
I gave him some sedatives, so he's still sleeping.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.480
Luckily, the bullet missed his major organs.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.780
But there's the possibility of infection.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.070
It would be better to check him into a hospital.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.160
Commander? The injection...

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.330
Even though he was alive during the war...

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.000
...Father never really experienced it firsthand.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.840
I guess he never knew what it feels like to kill a man.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.930
Raised during the war...

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.220
...he joined the SDF only after its conclusion.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.060
What could he possibly have known?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.560
Right now it's the 17th Showa year.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.820
My father is eight.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:03.530
Maybe, if I do get to visit the Japan of this era...

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.490
...I'll go meet him.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.370
I wonder what he thinks about this war.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.410
I'd really like to know.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.410
Commander.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.090
It's nothing serious. I'll be fine.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.130
That's good.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:27.720
Commander, the captain'd like to see you once you're awake.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.600
He wants Lieutenant Tsuda to be among the party...

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.640
...going ashore for the rescue operations.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.690
I heard that Lieutenant Katsuragi will be in charge.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.690
The captain would like you to pick 5 men to go along.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:45.780
The captain is replacing me with Katsuragi?!

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.450
I'll go... see him immediately!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.410
Yosuke.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.210
So it was an intense face off?

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.960
I can tell from the look on your face.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.470
How did it feel to take down your enemies?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.050
This is your first battle, right?

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.680
They weren't the enemy.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.640
They were Americans.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.310
Well, that's true for the Heisei Period.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.560
We're on the battle front now.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:25.860
In the Pacific war, Guadalcanal is a tragic island.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.320
To a journalist, however, it's a Treasure Island.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.240
I want to see it all!

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.200
I want to record the real truth!

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.660
If you go on land again...

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.620
...will you take me along as your cameraman?

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.380
He's thinking too much.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:51.550
It would be easier if he just considered them the enemy.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.060
Captain!

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.560
I feel I should go in place of Katsuragi!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.060
Listen to me, Commander.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.150
It's safer to send someone with prior experience.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.110
You're exhausted.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.110
I think you should rest some more.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.160
The 2500 Japanese engineers have not rested nor eaten...

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.450
...since their arrival in the jungle three days ago.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.040
I think they are far more exhausted than I am.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.420
Captain, I thank you for your concern.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.130
Nonetheless, I'm responsible for Yanagi, Kohei...

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.420
...and also the US Marines.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:30.010
The responsibility to prevent tragedy from repeating itself.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.180
I understand.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.140
I'll leave this in your hands.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.680
Thank you very much.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:14.220
That's the west of Guadalcanal, Cape Esperance.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.300
Yes.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.220
60 years later...

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.770
60 years later...

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:23.890
Does everyone think like you, Commander Kadomatsu?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.230
What do you mean?

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:29.440
You won the jungle battle with the US Marines.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.320
But you referred to it as a tragedy.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:37.030
I don't understand why you called it that.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:40.120
Kusaka has read about...

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.000
...how Japan came to be what it is.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.000
But you haven't.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.330
And that's why it's hard for you to understand.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.340
I wonder if Lieutenant Kusaka...

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.510
...can truly understand the members of Mirai.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.510
I don't know.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.300
He still let the Yamato launch the bombardment.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.010
Sometimes even I can't figure him out.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.140
15 yards to shore!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.140
Lowering speed. Stopping!

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:05.100
Mirai 01

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.720
According to history,

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:41.970
...almost all the Navy Engineers on Guadalcanal were killed.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.480
Get into platoon formation!

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:48.020
Keep marching! Watch your posture!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.020
All casualties to the front!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.530
Starting from now, history will be rewritten.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.160
Attention!

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:06.000
We're your receiving party.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.000
I'm the Commander of the Retreat Support Division.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.290
Lieutenant Tsuda!

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.790
Thank you. I'm Monzen.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.420
The 84th defense squadron.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:18.260
11th and 13th engineers divisions have arrived.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.890
I haven't seen those uniforms before.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.050
Who are they?

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:25.600
Unfortunately, their identity is classified information.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.600
They're with the special unit.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.440
I see.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:33.520
I assume that Lieutenant Okamura of the 13th squadron is with you?

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:36.860
I've also heard that there are 2,500 soldiers on land.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.490
Okamura?

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:42.700
He's a very capable man, who prefers to operate alone.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.950
He broke away from the main unit...

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.250
...and disappeared into the jungle with a few subordinates.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.750
Only 185 men out of the 2,500 total...

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.710
...were able to make it to this meeting point.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.180
The commands were interrupted by the attack.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.050
All 2500 soldiers were separated...

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:05.310
...as they scrambled into the jungle for safety.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:08.640
There should be more than a thousand survivors.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.350
But the perilous conditions do not permit a search.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.320
We have decided to leave them.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.360
I understand.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.320
Please hurry and board the boats so we can leave.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.490
We'll send you back to Truk Island.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.660
Thank you, Lieutenant!

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.700
All aboard now! Hurry up!

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.040
Hurry up! Casualties in front!

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.960
- Give me the signal set.
- Yes!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.960
Critical conditions in the centre, injured to the side.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.970
You guys wait for me here.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.470
Commander! Where're you going?!

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.220
Commander Kadomatsu?

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.400
Once the rescue party returns...

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.150
...we'll finally be able to set out for Truk.

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:03.280
You do realize that's the Combined Fleet's Base, right?

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.780
We'll worry about that later.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.580
Was it the right decision to let him go?

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.670
You mean Yosuke?

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:17.000
Yes. Did you see the look in his eyes?

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.250
He's not himself.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:21.010
You may be right.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.050
But I'm not myself either.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:26.140
When I think back on it, my hands start shaking.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.390
Then why did you permit him to?!

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:29.890
It's useless.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.810
Yosuke has never been one for advice.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:39.730
When he's in trouble or when he gets lost...

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:44.240
...he just goes on alone, never asking for help.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:48.240
He thinks and plows ahead until he bumps into the answer.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.160
That's exactly what he's doing now.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.750
He's always been doing it.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:58.670
Embracing uncertainty might also mean embracing death!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:01.840
That island is still a battlefield!

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.850
Even if I don't get them all,

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:18.230
finding one or two will be enough.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.860
If you're hiding around here, come on out!

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:42.050
Hold up!

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:50.010
Release your weapon.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.570
You look Japanese to me.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.700
Do you understand English?

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.950
Your pronunciation was really bad.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.540
I could tell you were Japanese right away.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.460
I see.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.460
I have to say, that's a pretty strange helmet.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.930
Are you with the Imperial Navy?

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:31.970
No. Not exactly.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.930
My name is Yosuke Kadomatsu.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:36.680
Very well.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.150
I'm with the 13th Engineers Division.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.440
My name's Okamura.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.530
Like I guessed, he commands...

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.530
...the engineers division on Guadalcanal Island.

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:50.200
Lieutenant Okamura.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.330
That's an interesting rifle you've got there.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.660
You can pick it up.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.200
Okay.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:03.210
By the way, Mr. Kadomatsu, why are you in a place like this?

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.920
I'm looking for engineers who are unaware of the orders for retreat.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:13.350
- There aren't any around here.
- But...

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.640
You're all back.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:24.310
Report! We have searched the area...

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.280
...but we could not find it.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.820
Good work! You guys've done a good job.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.660
We've no choice then. We've run out of time.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:34.200
I want you guys to head for the shore immediately.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.200
- The life boats are waiting.
- Yes!

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:41.210
- And you, Lieutenant?
- Me? I'm staying behind.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.500
Lieutenant! You can't!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.090
What are you going to do alone, Lieutenant?!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.090
Please let us come with you!

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:51.090
Absolutely not. You have your duties to fulfil.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.930
I want you to deliver a message to Commander Monzen.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:54.890
Yes!

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.220
Tell him that Okamura will be taking over...

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.270
...and bear full responsibility for the engineers division.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.640
Yes.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:04.100
Next thing, is the ship.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.400
Inform Lieutenant Monzen to send a ship.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:11.280
Pick up the remaining engineers from this beach in a week's time.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.530
You make sure you pick us up! You got that?!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.120
- Yes!
- Get going!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.410
Set off before sunrise or you'll be easy targets!

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:20.250
Yes sir!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.330
We will do everything in our power...

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.830
...to return to Truk and complete the mission!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:28.130
Good! And make sure you bring a huge ship!

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.670
Commander! Take care of yourself!

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.840
Let's go! Don't fall behind!

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.930
Yes!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.060
Mr. Kadomatsu.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.310
Aren't you going with them?

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.270
Why did you decide to stay back?

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.400
Because I've seen it.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.360
What have you seen?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.570
On my way here into the jungle...

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.910
...there was evidence of campfires residue everywhere.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.870
It proves that the engineers are still alive.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.750
They have no idea about the retreat order...

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.670
...still wandering in the jungle, hungry and shivering with fear.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:13.970
As long as I know that, I can't leave them behind.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:18.970
If I leave them, they'll encounter the US Marines and there'll be bloodshed.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.930
They aren't even armed.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.480
Two days ago...

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:30.610
I killed 8 US Marines with these hands of mine.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:35.030
Blood spilled for nothing. Nonetheless...

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.860
...there wasn't any choice then.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.280
Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:42.120
You happened to meet the enemy, right?

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:45.080
They're not the enemy!

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:48.250
I'm not from this era.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.840
I wasn't born in the 17th Showa year.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:57.010
I'm from a technologically advanced Japan...

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.970
...60 years in the future.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:04.600
Lieutenant, all the wounded have boarded.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.060
We're the only ones left.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.810
Lieutenant Tsuda, aren't you coming with us?

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:12.690
No. I have another mission.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:15.030
Is that so?

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.110
I see. We'll set off first then.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.740
Ready! Forward!

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.540
Commander! Take care!

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.090
We'll come back for you!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.340
That will do.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:42.390
Please contact the Mirai.

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.350
Yes!

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.060
Commander Kadomatsu...

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.400
We... the Imperial Navy, will complete the rescue operation.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:55.110
The responsibility to prevent history from repeating itself...

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:57.070
...shouldn't be a burden to be borne alone.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.320
You mean that...

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:05.240
...something tragic as that is what's in store for this island?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.540
According to the history I know.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:13.090
In a week's time, you will fight alongside Ichiki's Division.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:16.590
What's more, you will come out alive.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.340
I don't think, however, that they will be returning.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:24.470
I know it's hard for you to believe what I'm telling you.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:27.770
No, I believe you, Mr. Kadomatsu.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.940
I understand.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:35.270
You're just as bad as I am.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.820
You're the sort who can't lie to himself.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.650
Let alone lie to someone else.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.370
And you still choose to stay behind?

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:48.160
The Okamura in your history books...

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.960
...probably didn't have any regrets.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.420
I have to contact the rest of the engineers.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:59.550
Please excuse me.

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:27.620
Our involvement changes Okamura's path in history.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.580
Can I bear the responsibility as he does?

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.380
This altered history...

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.720
...is one I cannot run away from.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:59.070
The Navy is behaving very strangely...

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.740
...in the waters around Guadalcanal.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.780
Not only did they let the US Marines land on the island...

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:06.950
...but now they're running like cowards!

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.450
I wonder why.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:12.330
We'll lose Guadalcanal if this continues!

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.080
If the US Marines manage to occupy Guadalcanal...

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:21.050
...they'll completely disrupt the Port Moresby Operation!

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:25.550
That airstrip was the Navy's idea in the first place!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.430
And now... they're abandoning it?!

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:29.430
Exactly!

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:32.770
War is about two things: risk and spirit!

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.440
The army must protect Guadalcanal at all costs!

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:40.730
And the Navy will be indebted to us again.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:43.440
Let me deal with this.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:50.280
Your head hasn't fully healed yet.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:54.200
Oh this? Wouldn't you expect a front-line soldier...

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:57.000
...to have a wound or two?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.880
What are you proposing?

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:06.010
I... Masanobu Tsuji, will clarify this mystery behind the Imperial Navy.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:17.130
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:22.340
Just peacefully

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:34.150
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:47.030
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:53.670
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.240 --> 00:22:59.740
I kept on praying

00:23:01.110 --> 00:23:11.550
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.420 --> 00:23:27.230
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:42.390
There are a total of...

00:23:42.390 --> 00:23:46.180
...50,000 Japanese soldiers and civilians living here.

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:47.930
That's unthinkable in our era.

00:23:48.390 --> 00:23:52.810
For us, our era might as well be a thousand light years away.

00:23:52.810 --> 00:23:54.820
It may be Admiral Yamamoto's intention...

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:57.240
...to keep the knowledge of the Mirai to himself.

00:23:57.240 --> 00:23:59.240
Where are they leading us?

00:23:59.240 --> 00:24:01.240
The cards have been dealt.

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:04.910
Next Episode: Zipang Initiation

00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:04.200
Let me take you somewhere more appropriate.

00:24:04.910 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the characters and organizations that appear have no connections with actual people and organizations.
